! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260's CONSTANTS AND INTERRUPT TABLE --
! PDF p.86 (printed p.83), octal 023042.00-023070.00, transcribed
! VERBATIM at the listing's own addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_160k_listing.py.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  It is the harness the p.71 comparison driver needs
! (ax5b_160105_compare.strap), and it SETTLES THREE THINGS that
! earlier transcriptions in this project had to leave open or infer.
!
! 1. I60K7 IS THE ILLEGAL OP.  ax5b_16082_op_ad.strap SYN'd I60K7 from
!    "LX,$X4,I60K7 -> 23050.10 10" on p.41 and its header said, under
!    "NOT TRACED": "WHAT I60K7 CONTAINS.  Only its address, 023050.00,
!    is printed here.  The block's SHAPE ... reads like self-modifying
!    code planting an invalid operation code ... Nothing on these pages
!    says so."  p.86 says so:
!        I60K7  %8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740   -ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31.
!    The inference was right and is now a printed fact.
!
! 2. I60K16 IS "BD,I6086A", confirming the external
!    ax5b_16086_ds.strap SYN'd from p.43's "LX,$X4,I60K16".
!
! 3. THE INTERRUPT TABLE IS 64 WORDS, STATED RATHER THAN REASONED.
!        I60IT   DR%BU,64,8@,64    023201.00
!        I60DMP  XW,0,0,0,0        023301.00
!    023301 - 023201 = 0o100 = 64.  run_tests.sh's "The interruption
!    mechanism" section had REASONED the units were "64 full words,
!    from I60IT at 023201.00 to I60DMP at 023301.00"; the DR row
!    states the 64 directly.
!
! AND I60K12 IS THE TABLE'S DEFAULT ENTRY: "BD,I6010A" twice, so every
! interruption disables and branches to the label p.71 calls "-ALL
! INTRPTS EXCEPT AD ENTER HERE."  I60XW1 ("XW,0,64,I60IT" -- count 64,
! refill I60IT) is what the comparison driver's CB+ loop walks to copy
! it into all 64 slots.
!
! IT ALSO EXPOSED AN ASSEMBLER GAP, the third this routine has found.
! "C+I,$X1,I60DMP" at 023044.00 prints "23301.03 00" -- I60DMP's WORD
! address in bits 0-17 -- and the assembler evaluated the label to a
! BIT address and wrapped it.  Count-type immediates now use
! eval_addr_field with shift 6, exactly as XW's refill field already
! did: a label scales >>6, a bare integer counts words, so
! "LCI,$X1,18" is unchanged.  (The first two gaps: TRANSMIT/SWAP not
! encodable at all, found by p.45's TI; XW's fourth operand masked to
! one bit, found by I60S1's single XW row.)
!
! ENCODING ONLY: these are constants, with nothing to execute.  The
! rows past 023070.00 -- I60XW5-9, USAWD, USALVE, I60INT, I60IT,
! I60DMP, BOUND0, BOUND1 -- are not transcribed here; USALVE needs
! LVE and the DR reserves are better given to whatever program
! actually runs the table.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: none, where this header used to say "one.  Numeric
! labels prefixed L."  The prefix was there because this assembler
! reads a leading digit as an address and the leading glyph was read
! as a digit.  Measured at 600 dpi it is the LETTER I, so the pool's
! own names -- I60K1..I60K17, I60XW1..I60XW4, I60AD1..I60AD3,
! I60DMP, I60IT and the externals -- are legal STRAP-1 symbols as
! printed and are written unaltered (docs/listing_typography.md).
! Every external is given by SYN at the address this block's own rows
! print for it.

I60DMP SYN, (8)23301.0
I6035  SYN, (8)14642.0
I6090  SYN, (8)21512.40
I6097  SYN, (8)22072.0
I6010A SYN, (8)22371.40
I6086A SYN, (8)21372.40
I60107 SYN, (8)22372.0
I60IT  SYN, (8)23201.0
        SLC, (8)23042.0
I60K1  XW, (8)777777.60, 0, 0
I60K2  SX, $X1, I60DMP
        NOP
I60K3  C+I, $X1, I60DMP
        NOP
I60K4  SV, $X1, I60DMP
        NOP
I60K5  BD, I6035
        BD, I6035
I60K6  BD, I6090
        NOP
I60K7  DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740     ! -ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31.
        NOP
I60K8  BD, I6097
        NOP
I60K9  XW, -1.0, 0, 0
I60K10 XW, 1.0, 1, 0
I60K11 XW, -3.0, 63, 0
I60K12 BD, I6010A
        BD, I6010A
I60K13 NOP
        NOP
I60K14 XW, -0.1, 0, 0
I60K15 XW, -(8)777777.60, 0, 0
I60K16 BD, I6086A
        BD, I6086A
I60K17 BD, I60107
        BD, I60107
I60AD1 NOP
I60AD2 NOP
I60AD3 NOP
        NOP
I60XW1 XW, 0, 64, I60IT
I60XW2 XW, 0, 48, 0
I60XW3 XW, (8)101.0, 0, 0
I60XW4 XW, 0, 63, I60IT
        END, I60K1
